Changes made for march:

  * Bindings that invoke Omarchy's own binaries (omarchy-menu, omarchy-launch-*,
    omarchy-toggle-*, omarchy-capture-*, voxtype, ...) are either repointed at
    equivalents packaged for Arch Linux ARM or dropped. None of Omarchy's own
    packages are built for aarch64, so keeping them would produce shortcuts that
    silently do nothing.

  * The app launcher is fuzzel rather than walker: walker and its elephant
    backend have no aarch64 package.

  * Blur, shadows and animations are disabled. march's VMs have no GPU
    passthrough, so Mesa renders in software via llvmpipe and these effects cost
    far more than they are worth.

  * Laptop-only bindings (lid switch, touchpad toggles, keyboard backlight) are
    removed, having no meaning in a virtual machine.

  * Theme-switching machinery is omitted; march ships a single look.
